  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Digital Talent Activity</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="ES">Proyecto Talento Digital</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">(El Salvador):  El Salvador is currently experiencing exponential demand for information technology skills and English-speaking talent, such as developers, data analysts, digital marketing, and cybersecurity. The Digital Talent (DT) activity develops the technical competencies of students to meet the employment demands of the global digital industry. The activity focuses not only on developing IT skills (programming, coding, and data analysis) and business English skills, but also life skills and social-emotional support. It aims to reduce the digital divide in the public education system by providing students and teachers with exposure to innovative technologies and digital skill sets. It also supports promising youth to pursue higher education and gain access to employment opportunities in an emerging digital industry in El Salvador. With the support of USAID, Fundaci&amp;oacute;n Sagrera Palomo aims to maximize and enhance the current infrastructure of its training model-optimizing the use of the facilities in which the education centers operate- and to capitalize on the experience and technical capacity of the Digital Talent teaching staff acquired through the years, as well as relationships with private sector companies and foundations, public schools, universities, and local communities. This activity will develop the technical competencies of students to meet the employment demands of the digital industry -- specifically programming, coding, and data analysis. The DT activity contributes to ICS MO 3.2 and to RCS Pillar I by strengthening Salvadoran human capital&apos;s capacity to fill modern workforce needs. DT will also contribute to the Agency&apos;s localization agenda, particularly to the pillars related to shifting power to local actors and promoting space for them to influence and exercise leadership over priority setting, activity design and implementation, and measuring and evaluating results, and increasing funding through direct awards to local partners.</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="ES">trabajando de la mano con USAID, bajo la iniciativa Talento Digital, buscamos potenciar el talento local. Brindar a los j&#xF3;venes las herramientas necesarias, como conocimientos t&#xE9;cnicos en programaci&#xF3;n (IT), ingl&#xE9;s y valores para que una vez egresados &#x200B;&#x200B;puedan optar a oportunidades de educaci&#xF3;n superior y/o empleos que les permitan continuar con su proceso de desarrollo personal y profesional, contribuyendo de la mano al desarrollo social y econ&#xF3;mico de nuestro pa&#xED;s y regi&#xF3;n.</narrative>
  </description>
